From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 02:25:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: matisse3g: enable WCN3660 Bluetooth

The stock WCNSS firmware advertises APPS_RIVA_BT_CMD and APPS_RIVA_BT_ACL
on the already running SMD edge. Add the standard WCNSS Bluetooth child
so btqcomsmd can bind without UART attachment or Android userspace.
The per-device local-bd-address is supplied privately during packaging.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
@@ -241,6 +241,10 @@
 				qcom,smd-channels = "WCNSS_CTRL";
 				qcom,mmio = <&pronto>;
 				firmware-name = "qcom/matisse3g/WCNSS_qcom_wlan_nv.bin";
+
+				bluetooth {
+					compatible = "qcom,wcnss-bt";
+				};
 
 				wifi {
 					compatible = "qcom,wcnss-wlan";
